{{- if model.manifest.tenant_ready -}}
# Tenancy quick start: your first feature

Read this before you write any code that stores data. It takes about 10 minutes.

## The idea in one paragraph

This service keeps each customer's (tenant's) data apart inside one database. You never filter by tenant yourself.
You mark an entity as tenant-owned, and the platform does the rest: every read sees only the current tenant's rows,
every insert is stamped with the current tenant, and an update or delete can never touch another tenant's row.
The current tenant comes from configuration (single-tenant mode) or from the caller's access token (multi-tenant mode),
never from the request body, query string, route or a header. This service is in
**{{ if model.manifest.multi_tenancy }}multi-tenant{{ else }}single-tenant{{ end }}** mode. Your code is the same in both.

## Six steps

The example adds a `Projects` feature. Replace the names with yours.

### 1. The entity: derive from `TenantEntity<Guid>`

`src/{{ model.names.namespace }}/Domains/Projects/Data/Project.cs`

```csharp
using Pervaxis.Core.Data.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Data;

public sealed class Project : TenantEntity<Guid>
{
    public Project(Guid id, string code, string name)
    {
        Id = id;
        Code = code;
        Name = name;
    }

    public string Code { get; set; }

    public string Name { get; set; }
}
```

- Do **not** add a `TenantId` property. It comes from `TenantEntity`, and the platform sets it.
- Give the id yourself (`Guid.NewGuid()`). The key is `(TenantId, Id)`, which does not auto-generate.
- Data shared by all tenants (a list of countries, for example) is not tenant-owned: mark it `[SharedEntity]` instead.

### 2. The configuration: one class next to the entity

`src/{{ model.names.namespace }}/Domains/Projects/Data/ProjectConfiguration.cs`

```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Metadata.Builders;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Data;

public sealed class ProjectConfiguration : IEntityTypeConfiguration<Project>
{
    public void Configure(EntityTypeBuilder<Project> builder)
    {
        builder.ToTable("projects");
        builder.Property(p => p.Code).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(50);
        builder.Property(p => p.Name).IsRequired().HasMaxLength(200);

        // Unique per tenant: two tenants may both have project "P-1".
        builder.HasIndex("TenantId", nameof(Project.Code)).IsUnique();
    }
}
```

- It is picked up automatically by `{{ model.names.dot_net_class_name }}DbContext`. Do **not** create another `DbContext`:
  a separate one would not isolate tenants.
- A relationship between two tenant-owned entities uses a tenant-inclusive foreign key:
  `builder.HasOne(t => t.Project).WithMany().HasForeignKey("TenantId", nameof(ProjectTask.ProjectId));`
- A unique index must include `TenantId`. The service refuses to start if it does not.

### 3. The migration

```bash
dotnet ef migrations add AddProjects --project src/{{ model.names.namespace }} --output-dir Data/Migrations
dotnet ef database update --project src/{{ model.names.namespace }}
```

Commit the generated files. See [`Database.md`](Database.md) for how migrations reach test and production.

### 4. The service: use the repository

`src/{{ model.names.namespace }}/Domains/Projects/Services/ProjectService.cs`

```csharp
using Pervaxis.Core.Abstractions.Data;
using {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Data;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Services;

public interface IProjectService
{
    Task<Project?> GetAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken cancellationToken);

    Task<IReadOnlyList<Project>> ListAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken);

    Task<Project> CreateAsync(string code, string name, CancellationToken cancellationToken);
}

public sealed class ProjectService : IProjectService
{
    private readonly IRepository<Project, Guid> _projects;
    private readonly IUnitOfWork _unitOfWork;

    public ProjectService(IRepository<Project, Guid> projects, IUnitOfWork unitOfWork)
    {
        _projects = projects;
        _unitOfWork = unitOfWork;
    }

    // Only the current tenant's project. Another tenant's id simply returns null.
    public Task<Project?> GetAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
        => _projects.GetByIdAsync(id, cancellationToken);

    // Only the current tenant's projects.
    public Task<IReadOnlyList<Project>> ListAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
        => _projects.GetAllAsync(cancellationToken);

    public async Task<Project> CreateAsync(string code, string name, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var project = new Project(Guid.NewGuid(), code, name);
        await _projects.AddAsync(project, cancellationToken);   // TenantId is stamped on save
        await _unitOfWork.CommitAsync(cancellationToken);
        return project;
    }
}
```

Register it in `Extensions/ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs`:

```csharp
services.AddScoped<IProjectService, ProjectService>();
```

`IRepository<,>` and `IUnitOfWork` are already registered for every tenant-owned entity.

### 5. The endpoint: no tenant in the request

`src/{{ model.names.namespace }}/Domains/Projects/Controllers/ProjectsController.cs`

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
using {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Services;

namespace {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Controllers;

public sealed record CreateProjectRequest(string Code, string Name);   // no TenantId here, ever

public sealed record ProjectResponse(Guid Id, string Code, string Name);

[ApiController]
[Route("{{ model.names.api_base_route }}/projects")]
public sealed class ProjectsController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IProjectService _projects;

    public ProjectsController(IProjectService projects) => _projects = projects;

    [HttpGet("{id:guid}")]
    public async Task<IActionResult> GetAsync(Guid id, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var project = await _projects.GetAsync(id, cancellationToken);
        return project is null ? NotFound() : Ok(new ProjectResponse(project.Id, project.Code, project.Name));
    }

    [HttpGet]
    public async Task<IActionResult> ListAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken)
        => Ok((await _projects.ListAsync(cancellationToken)).Select(p => new ProjectResponse(p.Id, p.Code, p.Name)));

    [HttpPost]
    public async Task<IActionResult> CreateAsync([FromBody] CreateProjectRequest request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
    {
        var project = await _projects.CreateAsync(request.Code, request.Name, cancellationToken);
        return Created($"{{ model.names.api_base_route }}/projects/{project.Id}", new ProjectResponse(project.Id, project.Code, project.Name));
    }
}
```

The platform answers for you: another tenant's project is **404**, a missing tenant is **403**,
and a concurrent edit is **409**. Do not catch these.

### 6. The test: prove tenant A cannot see tenant B

`tests/{{ model.names.test_project_name }}/ProjectIsolationTests.cs`

```csharp
using FluentAssertions;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Pervaxis.Core.Abstractions.MultiTenancy;
using {{ model.names.namespace }}.Data;
using {{ model.names.namespace }}.Domains.Projects.Data;
using Xunit;

namespace {{ model.names.test_project_name }};

public sealed class ProjectIsolationTests : IDisposable
{
    private static readonly TenantId TenantA = new(Guid.NewGuid().ToString("D"));
    private static readonly TenantId TenantB = new(Guid.NewGuid().ToString("D"));

    // In-memory SQLite with this service's schema (see TenantManagementTests.cs).
    private readonly TenantTestDatabase _database = new();
    private readonly ServiceProvider _services;

    public ProjectIsolationTests() => _services = _database.BuildServices();

    private async Task<int> CountAsync(TenantId tenant)
    {
        using var scope = _services.CreateScope();
        using var asTenant = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ITenantScopeFactory>().BeginScope(tenant);
        var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<{{ model.names.dot_net_class_name }}DbContext>();
        return await db.Set<Project>().CountAsync();
    }

    [Fact]
    public async Task EachTenant_SeesOnlyItsOwnProjects()
    {
        using (var scope = _services.CreateScope())
        using (scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<ITenantScopeFactory>().BeginScope(TenantA))
        {
            var db = scope.ServiceProvider.GetRequiredService<{{ model.names.dot_net_class_name }}DbContext>();
            db.Add(new Project(Guid.NewGuid(), "P-1", "Apollo"));
            await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        }

        (await CountAsync(TenantA)).Should().Be(1);
        (await CountAsync(TenantB)).Should().Be(0);
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _services.Dispose();
        _database.Dispose();
    }
}
```

## Checklist before every pull request

- [ ] Every new entity derives from `TenantEntity<TId>`, or is marked `[SharedEntity]` on purpose.
- [ ] No `TenantId` in any request model, route, query string or header.
- [ ] Relationships between tenant-owned entities use `HasForeignKey("TenantId", ...)`.
- [ ] Unique indexes include `TenantId`.
- [ ] A migration was added and committed.
- [ ] Data access goes through `IRepository<,>` or `{{ model.names.dot_net_class_name }}DbContext`. No new `DbContext`.
- [ ] No `IgnoreQueryFilters()` without names, `FromSql*`, `ExecuteSql*`, `ExecuteUpdate` or `ExecuteDelete` on tenant-owned data.
- [ ] No single-key `Find`/`FindAsync` on tenant-owned entities.
- [ ] Background jobs wrap each unit of work in `ITenantScopeFactory.BeginScope(tenantId)`.
- [ ] Cache keys and file paths for tenant data include `ITenantContext.TenantId` (read it, never take it from the request).
- [ ] A test proves another tenant cannot see the new data.

## When you need the current tenant in code

Usually you do not. If you do (cache keys, logs, calls to other systems), inject `ITenantContext`:

```csharp
public sealed class ReportService(ITenantContext tenant)
{
    private string CacheKey(string report) => $"reports:{tenant.TenantId.Value}:{report}";
}
```

Never pass the tenant as a method parameter that a caller could fill from a request.

